      1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَاخَتِ الرِّيحُ</span></b> , aor. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَفِيخُ</span>, inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيْخٌ</span> and

<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيَخَانٌ</span>: see 1 in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فوخ</span>. Accord. to Kr and
the K, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَيْخٌ</span> signifies <i>A spreading,</i> or <i>becoming diffused;</i> like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فِيْحٌ</span>: (TA:) but ISd expresses doubt
of the correctness of this: (L, TA:) it is [said
to be] an inf. n. in this sense. (TK.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  See
also 4.

